<title>USA: Democrats open convention to re-nominate Clinton.</title>
<headline>Democrats open convention to re-nominate Clinton.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Democratic Party on Monday opened a four-day convention that will formally nominate President Bill Clinton for a second term.</p>
<p>The convention was called to order shortly after 5 p.m. EDT (2100 GMT). It will culminate on Thursday when Clinton delivers a speech accepting re-nomination to face Republican nominee Bob Dole in the November 5 election.</p>
</text>
